<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Squamous cell carcinoma of the right tonsillar pillar, p16-negative, suspected at presentation and confirmed by biopsy at the otolaryngology visit; linked to the documented 1885 diagnosis: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Nicotine dependence, cigars, about ten a day for more than forty years: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Painful swallowing with oropharyngeal dysphagia from the tonsillar tumor: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Unintended weight loss from painful swallowing, about 2 kg before presentation and 9% of body weight by the end of treatment: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Varenicline 1 mg oral tablet, one tablet twice daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Acetaminophen 160 mg/5 mL oral solution, 20 mL (640 mg) every 6 hours as needed for throat pain [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Lidocaine viscous 2% solution, 15 mL swish and spit up to every 3 hours as needed for throat pain [S]</item><item>Goal: Tissue diagnosis within two weeks of the first visit. Outcome by 2026-07-21: Biopsy at the otolaryngology visit two weeks after presentation [S]</item><item>Goal: Stop all tobacco use before treatment begins. Outcome by 2026-08-04: No cigars since mid-July 2026; varenicline continued [S]</item><item>Goal: Limit weight loss to less than 10% of baseline weight through treatment. Outcome by 2026-10-22: Weight 71.0 kg, 9% below the 78.0 kg baseline [S]</item><item>Goal: Keep throat pain at 4 or below on the 0-10 scale most days. Outcome by 2026-10-22: Pain score 3 of 10 [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 2026-07-07 [S]</item><item>Scheduled episode complete. Continue routine follow-up [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
